// PARAM: --analysis sign
// REFUTED counterpart of 01-straight_line_sign.vimp: an exact negative write
// settles the same condition the other way. Sign carries no magnitude, but
// the sign alone decides 0 < x in both directions, so the pair pins that
// sign_lt refutes as precisely as it proves -- a one-sided fixture would let
// a regression that collapses every comparison to PROVED go unnoticed.
//
// The write is a negative literal rather than 0 - 5 on purpose: an
// arithmetic node norms its result at its kind, and Sign cannot certify a
// negative abstract value fits int32, so the subtraction would top. That is
// known-imprecision/01, and it is not what this fixture is about.

void main() {
  int32 x;
  x := -5;
  __voblint_check(0 < x) // REFUTED
}
